{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires","id":888775,"title":"Silver Record explanation for vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-11T19:40:11-07:00","id":888775,"title":"Silver Record explanation for vampires","content":"Can somebody give me the basics of the Garou legend on the origin of vampires as it was told in the Silver Record? I believe it mentioned something about the Eater of Souls and Helios.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:55:22-07:00","id":888785,"title":"","content":"Basic version: Weaver fell in love with a man made him perfect and immortal. Wyrm trying to do his job eats him vampire to be feeds on Wyrm. Wyrm vomits new vampire out Helios sees him and blasts him.<br /> <br /> And the Garou haven't realized the Weaver is the real bad guy why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:12:42-07:00","id":888970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=888785#post888785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basic version: Weaver fell in love with a man made him perfect and immortal. Wyrm trying to do his job eats him vampire to be feeds on Wyrm. Wyrm vomits new vampire out Helios sees him and blasts him.<br /> <br /> And the Garou haven't realized the Weaver is the real bad guy why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Good and Bad are kinda beyond the scope of the Triat. Also, while Weaver is an asshole, he's not activley trying to murder everything and corrupt everything that's sane. Sure, its machinations are dangerous, and probably should be stopped (and the books actually tell us the Garou fight the Weaver too), but at the end of the day it's just not a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:23:40-07:00","id":889131,"title":"","content":"Weaver spun in Wyrm, which in turn made Wyrm go mad and shizophrenic... so who's the evil now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T01:31:46-07:00","id":889743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=889131#post889131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver spun in Wyrm, which in turn made Wyrm go mad and shizophrenic... so who's the evil now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaver did what Weaver is. It tried to control things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:39:48-07:00","id":889935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=889131#post889131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver spun in Wyrm, which in turn made Wyrm go mad and shizophrenic... so who's the evil now?</div> </div> </div> </div>How many Garou sat around to listen to this when they were pressured into taking up arms and fighting? And then, after fighting beings of the Wyrm but not, say, encountering Drones, how does one imagine they'd react to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T03:08:22-07:00","id":893928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=889131#post889131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver spun in Wyrm, which in turn made Wyrm go mad and shizophrenic... so who's the evil now?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=889743#post889743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver did what Weaver is. It tried to control things.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about<b></b>: Weaver spun in the Wyrm for a little while so he'd <i><b>calm down just a little bit</b></i>.<br /> <br /> (It became problematic because the Wyrm then started becoming the hydra, and the situation became unsalvageable when the Wyld-aspected part of the Wyrm emerged: the Defiler Wyrm.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:19:09-07:00","id":893998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=893928#post893928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about<b></b>: Weaver spun in the Wyrm for a little while so he'd <i><b>calm down just a little bit</b></i>.<br /> <br /> (It became problematic because the Wyrm then started becoming the hydra, and the situation became unsalvageable when the Wyld-aspected part of the Wyrm emerged: the Defiler Wyrm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Defiler is the Triatic Wyrm generated from the Wyrm's own twisted self-image. The Beast-of-War is the Triatic Wyrm that arose from its broken recollection of the Wyld (at no point are any of them Wyld-aspected, just filtered ideas).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:56:03-07:00","id":894017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=893998#post893998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Defiler is the Triatic Wyrm generated from the Wyrm's own twisted self-image. The Beast-of-War is the Triatic Wyrm that arose from its broken recollection of the Wyld (at no point are any of them Wyld-aspected, just filtered ideas).</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I haven't read most of Werewolf books...<br /> And I know this is the way it is said.<br /> However, after reading the description of Seventh Generation in the New York book, I can't help but consider it the other way around. Basically, the Wyrm's twisted self-image is Beast of War (which can still have the corruptor bent...note that many of Fomori and Wyrm servitors indeed personify corruption combined with spiralling towards destruction) Defiler Wyrm is Wyrm filtered through trying to emulate Wyld in a sick way. This is the only way I can explain the general weirdness - and how pathetic and weak they are - of the Seventh Generation - the supposedly extremely dangerous and successful Cult of the Defiler.<br /> <br /> This also makes sense to me from a top-down design point of view...If Wyrm was a force of measured destruction, then it's later aspect that is linked most to itself (the Wyrmish part of the Wyrm) should be bent towards destruction more than corruption. The corruptor (and defilement) elements actually fit perfectly as coming from the Wyld. Madness, mutation, crazy (and often useless) wisdom are where the Wyldish Wyrm (Defiler Wyrm in my outlook) and the Wyld overlap.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it odd that the Wyldish part of the Triatic Wyrm would focus as a force called Beast-of-War. Too directed; and destruction is not the only expression of uncontrollable, limitless change that you could say Wyld could be perceived as under a bad light.<br /> Defiler Wyrm as the Wyldish Wyrm fits more for me.<br /> <br /> (One of the reasons the Defiler Wyrm has such a horrible effect on humans could be because Wyld definitely doesn't want to do much with civilized, power-hungry humans. So many cultists of the Defiler Wyrm become insane as a function of literally calling on a power they shouldn't...but not in any way that is beneficial to them, most of time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-19-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:48:28-07:00","id":894111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888775-silver-record-explanation-for-vampires?p=894017#post894017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I haven't read most of Werewolf books...<br /> And I know this is the way it is said.<br /> However, after reading the description of Seventh Generation in the New York book, I can't help but consider it the other way around. Basically, the Wyrm's twisted self-image is Beast of War (which can still have the corruptor bent...note that many of Fomori and Wyrm servitors indeed personify corruption combined with spiralling towards destruction) Defiler Wyrm is Wyrm filtered through trying to emulate Wyld in a sick way. This is the only way I can explain the general weirdness - and how pathetic and weak they are - of the Seventh Generation - the supposedly extremely dangerous and successful Cult of the Defiler.<br /> <br /> This also makes sense to me from a top-down design point of view...If Wyrm was a force of measured destruction, then it's later aspect that is linked most to itself (the Wyrmish part of the Wyrm) should be bent towards destruction more than corruption. The corruptor (and defilement) elements actually fit perfectly as coming from the Wyld. Madness, mutation, crazy (and often useless) wisdom are where the Wyldish Wyrm (Defiler Wyrm in my outlook) and the Wyld overlap.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it odd that the Wyldish part of the Triatic Wyrm would focus as a force called Beast-of-War. Too directed; and destruction is not the only expression of uncontrollable, limitless change that you could say Wyld could be perceived as under a bad light.<br /> Defiler Wyrm as the Wyldish Wyrm fits more for me.<br /> <br /> (One of the reasons the Defiler Wyrm has such a horrible effect on humans could be because Wyld definitely doesn't want to do much with civilized, power-hungry humans. So many cultists of the Defiler Wyrm become insane as a function of literally calling on a power they shouldn't...but not in any way that is beneficial to them, most of time.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Calamity Wyrm is not particularly directed. It's the part of the Wyrm that's trying the hardest to struggle away from the Weaver's bindings in any way that it can, so by that antithetical association, Wyld association it is, while the Defiler is the Wyrm seeing itself as having failed and thus having to take up... new duties in its bindings, with no expectation that it will ever be free again. So, instead of destroying, it shits on the cosmos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}